    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "There is no higher crime than abuse of power. In fact, that includes a whole range of activities, including bribery, potentially. But abuse of power. Thank you, Rhode Island. Know that? Yeah, well, I mean, they're going to see that during the course of the presentation of the evidence, both at the Judiciary Committee and hopefully in the Senate. But this was what our framers spoke about when they spoke about articles of impeachment. The Constitution is the supreme law of the land. So violations of the Constitution is a crime. It's a constitutional crime. Why not say bribery? Well, because this is much worse. Abusive power is worse and it includes bribery and a range of other activities using the power of your office to advance your own political or personal interest and not the public interest. The framers spoke about using that office and they talk about foreign interference and about corrupting elections. And so abusive power is actually the worst. This is the president using the enormous powers of his office to corrupt an American election to cheat in 2020 and using the hundreds of millions of dollars of tax bear money as leverage to a core say foreign leader to help him cheat. And this is a crime in progress. You know, Rudy Giuliani just came back from Ukraine. This is ongoing. And that's why",
