    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "Well, that's, look, nobody runs for Congress. Nobody comes to Congress saying I'm here to impeach a president. You know, we ran on the agenda about driving down healthcare costs, raising family incomes, rebuilding the infrastructure of America, taking on the corruption in Washington and getting government to work for the people again. We've passed nearly 400 pieces of legislation, 275 bipartisan bills that do many of those things that are sitting on Mitch McConnell's desk. That's why we ran for Congress. Nobody comes in to do that, but we have no choice. When you're confronted with the president of the United States attempting to corrupt our elections, the single most important responsibility we have, we take an oath when we start. I will protect and defend the Constitution. We have no choice. So this is a responsibility we have. The times have found us. Nobody's happy about it. But we owe it to This generation into future generations, when they look back, we need to be able to say we did everything we could to protect our democracy, to be sure that people in this country get to elect their own president, and we've ensured that someone who tries to drag a foreign power into this is prevented from doing that.",
